   "issue": "`exists_contDiff_ae_eq_and_neg_laplacian_add_mul_eq` assumes `hweak : \u2200 \u03c6, ContDiff \u211d 2 \u03c6 \u2192 HasCompactSupport \u03c6 \u2192 ...`. The proof only applies `hweak` to `\u03c6 : \ud835\udcd3(\u22a4, \u211d)`, which are smooth (`hweak \u03c6 h\u03c62 \u03c6.hasCompactSupport`). The hypothesis is therefore stronger than needed, and callers that know the weak equation only against smooth test functions cannot use the theorem.",
